(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_chemistry_amines=[{id:"neet-2026-q048",pn:48,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun \xB7 Re-exam",tp:"Amines",st:"Basicity of substituted anilines",q:`Given below are two statements:
Statement-I: Oxidation of p-nitrotoluene with acidic KMnO\u2084 gives an acid that is stronger than benzoic acid.
Statement-II: Reduction of p-nitrotoluene with Sn/HCl followed by neutralization gives an amine that is more basic than aniline.
In light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.`,o:["Both Statement-I and Statement-II are incorrect","Statement-I is correct but Statement-II is incorrect","Statement-I is incorrect but Statement-II is correct","Both Statement-I and Statement-II are correct"],c:3,s:`Acidic KMnO\u2084 oxidises the \u2013CH\u2083 group of p-nitrotoluene to \u2013COOH, giving p-nitrobenzoic acid.
The \u2013NO\u2082 group has \u2013I and \u2013M effects, so p-nitrobenzoic acid is a stronger acid than benzoic acid. Statement-I is correct.
Sn/HCl reduces \u2013NO\u2082 to \u2013NH\u2082, giving p-toluidine (p-methylaniline).
The \u2013CH\u2083 group has +I effect and hyperconjugation, so p-methylaniline is more basic than aniline. Statement-II is correct.`},{id:"neet-2026-q070",pn:70,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun \xB7 Re-exam",tp:"Amines",st:"Preparation of aniline",q:`Identify the reactions which give aniline as the major product.
A. Benzonitrile (C\u2086H\u2085CN) with LiAlH\u2084
B. Benzamide (C\u2086H\u2085CONH\u2082) with KOH, Br\u2082
C. Nitrobenzene (C\u2086H\u2085NO\u2082) with NaBH\u2084
D. Acetanilide (C\u2086H\u2085NHCOCH\u2083) with HCl, H\u2082O, \u0394
Choose the correct answer from the options given below.`,o:["B and D only","A and C only","C and D only","A and B only"],c:0,s:`A: benzonitrile with LiAlH\u2084 gives benzylamine (C\u2086H\u2085CH\u2082NH\u2082), not aniline.
B: benzamide with KOH/Br\u2082 (Hofmann bromamide) gives aniline.
D: acid hydrolysis of acetanilide gives aniline.
So B and D give aniline.`},{id:"neet-2026-q083",pn:83,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun \xB7 Re-exam",tp:"Amines",st:"Grignard reagent with amines",q:`One of the products formed in the following reaction is
cyclohexyl\u2013MgBr + cyclohexyl\u2013NH\u2082 \u2192`,o:["2-aminobicyclohexyl (two cyclohexane rings joined by a single bond, NH\u2082 on a ring carbon next to the junction)","bicyclohexyl (two cyclohexane rings joined by a single bond)","cyclohexane","dicyclohexylamine (two cyclohexane rings joined through NH)"],c:2,s:`Grignard reagents react with amines by taking a proton from N\u2013H.
The carbon of cyclohexyl\u2013MgBr (carbanion-like, \u03B4\u2212) takes H from the NH\u2082 group.
This gives cyclohexane as the hydrocarbon product.`}]})();
